{title: Sing To The Lord A New Song}
{subtitle: Psalms 96:1–3}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 82}
{time: 6/8}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Gm7] |
| [Gm7] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [F7] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Sing to the LORD a new [Gm]song
Call out to [Eb]all the earth [Bb][F]
[Bb]Sing to the LORD and bless his [Gm]name
His sal[Eb]vation [F7]is so [Bb]dear
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Proclaim his sal[Gm]vation day after [Dm]day
Declare his [Eb]glory among the [Bb]na[F]tions
His [Eb]wonders shown to all peo[Gm]ples
Great is the [Eb]LORD in [F]praise [Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He is to be feared above all [Gm]gods
For all the [Eb]gods of the peo[Bb]ples [F]
Are [Bb]idols and nothing [Gm]more
But [Eb]the LORD [F]made the [Bb]heavens
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Proclaim his sal[Gm]vation day after [Dm]day
Declare his [Eb]glory among the [Bb]na[F]tions
His [Eb]wonders shown to all peo[Gm]ples
Great is the [Eb]LORD in [F]praise
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Splendor and [Eb]majesty [Gm]before him
Strength and [Eb]beauty [F]in his sanctuary
{end_of_verse}
